WEBVTT

00:00:59.116 --> 00:01:02.086
through a chemical reaction 
called photosynthesis.

00:01:02.086 --> 00:01:04.726
This process uses energy 
from sunlight

00:01:04.726 --> 00:01:08.266
to convert water and carbon dioxide 
into oxygen

00:01:08.266 --> 00:01:11.056
and energy-storing carbohydrates.

00:01:11.056 --> 00:01:15.056
Plants then consume 
these carbohydrates in a reverse process

00:01:15.056 --> 00:01:17.876
called respiration, 
converting them to energy

00:01:17.876 --> 00:01:21.166
and releasing carbon 
back into the atmosphere.

00:01:21.166 --> 00:01:25.381
In trees, however, a large portion
of that carbon isn’t released,

00:01:25.381 --> 00:01:29.717
and instead, is stored 
as newly formed wood tissue.

00:01:29.717 --> 00:01:33.577
During their lifetimes, 
trees act as carbon vaults,